            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Evgeni,\r\nI would like to swap your lsp omnifunc used by default for the following case:\r\n1. Use the Mini.completion mechanism of automatically triggering completion on keystrokes,\r\n2. Displaying the results in the native menu,\r\n3. Provide my own omnifunc function that will:\r\n** Read the current line and parse it,\r\n** Get the context and find completion results,\r\n** Return them in the Neovim expected format.\r\n\r\nI tried the following:\r\n```lua\r\nrequire(mini.completion').setup({\r\n  lsp_completion = {\r\n    source_func = 'omnifunc',\r\n    auto_setup = false\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n-- Use custom omnifunc.\r\nvim.bo.omnifunc = 'v:lua.bufferOmnifunc'\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe `bufferOmnifunc` is very simple. It is an Neovim global function with 2 parameters just like the default omnifunc that writes to a log file just to check if it i sbeing used.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately it looks like it is not being picked. The require call is in the `ftplugin/xxxx.lua` file.\r\n\r\nThank you for your time and effort...\r\n",
