            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I asked about my case for I assumed that once I stick to the omnifunc or completefunc signiture and return type format Mini.completion will be able to function like a completion popup manager.\r\n\r\nSorry, not quite. The best approach I can think of is the one from previous comment.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> Will it disable the mechanism or I need to apply the config you suggested to disable automatic setup. We would need to handle the fallback case as well for it uses the standard keys.\r\n\r\nSetting this variable to `true` will completely disable all 'mini.completion' functionality for that particular buffer. If you want to rely on its functionality in any way (like described earlier), I'd suggest not use it.\r\n\r\nAlso, as this seems out of scope for 'mini.completion' features right now, I'll move this to Discussions. Feel free to continue asking question, though. Happy to help!",
